Package: nestedtune
Title: Nested Cross-Validation for 'tidymodels'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jeffrey", "Girard", , "jeffgirard@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates how well a model tuning procedure performs on new
    data, by nested cross-validation. An inner resampling loop tunes the
    model with 'tune' or 'finetune'. An outer loop scores each tuned model on
    rows that the tuning did not see, as in Varma and Simon (2006)
    <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-7-91>. The package supports grid search, Bayesian
    optimization, racing, simulated annealing, fixed models and sets of
    models from 'workflowsets'. A separate function runs the procedure on all
    the data to fit the final model. The outer folds can run in parallel with
    'mirai'. The nested resampling constructor makes the same splits as
    nested_cv() from 'rsample', but it stores row indices in place of a copy
    of the data for each outer fold.
